type_former_capability UNDECLARED=0 SUPPORTED=1 DEFERRED=2 NOT_APPLICABLE=3 fields=RELATION_TYPE_ACTION,TERM_ACTION,ORDINARY_REINDEX,PURITY,IDENTITY_COMPUTATION,TRANSPORT,LIFTING,RESOURCE_HOOK,ARTIFACT

An internal relation-family goal is immutable and is identified by category, exact
left and right carrier IS_TYPE Claims, exact left and right HAS_TYPE Claims,
and Context bridge. The two carrier Claims may differ for dependent fibers;
unsupported heterogeneous carrier action is residual, not an invalid goal.
A goal stores no selected rule, search state, source position, conversion cache,
or object witness.

Action requests are immutable and graph-consed by their complete typed keys.
Action results are separate records keyed by request ID. A request is never
solved by mutating its identity. Context, Substitution, Operation, Claim,
Derivation, action, certificate, and compiler-work IDs never occur in object
Term identity.

OBJECT_TERM is the object-language `ap_t` action. Its request selects one
ordinary HAS_TYPE source Claim, one OBJECT_IDENTITY Context bridge, and the
exact IDENTITY_TYPE_COMPUTATION request for the source classifier. Its
certificate retains the two reindexed endpoint Claims, the instantiated
ordinary identity-family Claim, and an ordinary witness Term/HAS_TYPE Claim.
It is distinct from TERM, which remains the compiler-local PARAMETRIC_ACTION
term action. Neither action ID occurs in the witness Term identity.

A Context bridge is one shared span representation for endpoint substitutions.
Its certificate has an explicit semantic kind. EMPTY_IDENTITY is the unique
empty-telescope identity. PARAMETRIC_RELATION means each non-empty extension is
classified by the compiler-local relation action and cannot authorize object
identity. OBJECT_IDENTITY marks an extension classified by an exact computed
identity family and ordinary Context-binding witness Claim. Its action
certificate must be IDENTITY_TYPE_COMPUTATION; replay rejects a relation-action
certificate in that slot. The graph shape alone never upgrades
PARAMETRIC_RELATION to OBJECT_IDENTITY. The executable cases extend an object
bridge by a closed homogeneous carrier and compute the eight-boundary square
family for generated identity datatypes with nullary or nondependent fields.
General dependent fiber lifting remains residual.

CONSTANT_FAMILY_LIFT is the type-side computation law ap_const(delta)=refl.
For a closed carrier family A weakened into a non-empty object bridge, it
reuses the type-former-directed identity computation selected in the empty
Context and forms its endpoint Context and exact Claims over that bridge.
Generated ADT and pure-Return identities retain their generated declaration;
nondependent pure Pi retains its direct pointwise identity family and its three
pointwise Binding identities. It is not general dependent lifting.
INDEXED_HIGHER_LIFT acts on IdA(x0,x1) over the six-face bridge of its
endpoint Context. It generates an eight-index higher identity datatype: four
corner values, two vertical endpoint proofs, and two horizontal Context-bridge
proofs. A constructor exists only when all eight boundary faces specialize a
source identity constructor coherently. For each nondependent source field the
higher constructor has nine fields: four corner values, four edge identities,
and one field-square center. This is genuine square-center computation, but it
does not yet lift a later field classifier that depends on earlier fields.

For Gamma |- A type, Type action first constructs
Gamma^R.x0:A[pi0].x1:A[pi1]. Its relation type is formed in that endpoint
Context. A Type result contains the endpoint Context, both endpoint bindings,
the relation type Term, a nested pure-family abstraction over both endpoint
bindings, PARAMETRIC_ACTION semantics, its exact IS_TYPE Claim, and Context
certificates. PARAMETRIC_ACTION is rejected if presented as another semantic
kind; it does not certify object identity. The abstraction
uses the same THUNK(LAMBDA(...RETURN...)) representation as every dependent Pi
codomain family; it is not a HOTT-specific function tag. Certificate replay
checks the family body against the endpoint relation under an explicit
two-binding alpha correspondence.

Relation instantiation is one typed operation shared by diagonal Term action
and arbitrary-endpoint candidate materialization. It reindexes the exact left
and right endpoint and carrier Claims through the bridge, constructs the two
endpoint extensions and their CwF certificates, specializes the relation body,
and publishes its exact IS_TYPE Claim. Candidate materialization returns an
exact witness Claim, EMPTY_FAMILY, or RESIDUAL; a READY family plan alone is
never reported as a witness.

The first-fragment compiler forms are RELATION_TYPE(A0,A1,a0,a1) and
RELATION_WITNESS(a0,a1). They encode the current relational action only.
They are not yet object-language homogeneous identity: the type form does not
retain a selected relation between A0 and A1, and the endpoint-only witness
does not retain proof payload. The ap operation is a typed compiler action that
generates exact HAS_TYPE Derivations. A diagonal action may generate an
RELATION_WITNESS Term. The action of a Context variable is the corresponding
relation binding already present in the Context bridge. A witness Term stores
no action ID and is not evidence without its Derivation. Artifact persistence
and the interpretation as reflexivity remain deferred until the A1.T0
relation-to-identity gate replaces these provisional object forms.

Type-action dispatch is selected by one declarative type-former descriptor.
Ordinary ADTs, pure Pi, pure Comp, pure Thunk, and RELATION_HIGHER are
admitted. Universe and host primitive actions are explicitly unsupported;
effectful and unresolved computation rows are residual.

Admission currently means that the internal-parametricity relation action is
implemented. IDENTITY_COMPUTATION, TRANSPORT, and LIFTING are independent
capabilities. IDENTITY_COMPUTATION is SUPPORTED for closed ordinary ADTs whose
constructor fields are nondependent and whose field identity declarations are
available; a recursive field uses the identity declaration currently being
generated. It is also SUPPORTED for one exact fiber of a parameter-free indexed
ADT when every admitted source constructor is nullary and its result classifier
is exactly that fiber. This indexed-nullary rule admits identity computation on
the generated IdBool(false,false) family itself. It is SUPPORTED for
ThunkType(Comp(empty,A)) when the identity of A is available and for the listed
nondependent pure Pi pointwise fragment. TRANSPORT and general LIFTING remain
DEFERRED for every former in fragment version 4. A descriptor must not be
interpreted as complete Higher Observational Identity support until the
relevant lifting operations and their higher instances are implemented and
their object terms and computation rules have been replayed by the kernel.

For a nondependent pure computation function Pi(A,Comp(empty,B)), object
identity on ThunkType(Pi(...)) computes directly to the value type of a
three-argument pointwise proof over x0:A, x1:A, and IdA(x0,x1). Its result is
the identity between the thunked applications of the forced endpoint
functions. This direct computed Pi type is not wrapped in a generated
one-constructor declaration. Dependent codomains remain deferred until family
lifting is implemented.
The computation certificate retains the three pointwise Binding identities of
the identity template; accepted replay reconstructs no fresh binder and mutates
no semantic arena. Endpoint specialization may alpha-intern with an existing
concrete family that uses different physical Binding IDs. Object proof
construction therefore reads the three binders from the specialized family
graph and never requires them to equal the template Binding IDs.

IDENTITY_TYPE_COMPUTATION is a distinct action kind keyed by the exact source
IS_TYPE Claim and Context bridge. It does not depend on a preceding
RELATION_TYPE request: the parametricity relation is not authority for object
identity. It is never interned as the same request as RELATION_TYPE. Until a
type former has an ordinary generated identity-family graph and exact typing
Claim, execution publishes DEFERRED_OBJECT_RULE with no certificate.

UNIVERSE_FIBER is the first bridge-selected dependent identity rule. If an
object Context bridge for Gamma,A:Universe retains an exact Universe identity
witness whose correspondence projection is R:A0->A1->Universe, identity
computation for the following fiber b:A is R(b0,b1). The dispatcher selects
this rule from the preceding OBJECT_IDENTITY bridge certificate before it
consults the syntactic type-former descriptor for A. It never substitutes the
compiler-local PARAMETRIC_ACTION relation. Context weakening and substitution
reindex preserve their exact premise Claims and semantic substitution edges.
The object-telescope driver recursively ensures the parent object bridge,
executes the exact identity computation selected by each Context-formation
Claim, and extends the bridge only from a READY object certificate. The rule
therefore repeats across every supported Context extension. A valid but
unsupported fiber publishes a residual result and never falls back to a
PARAMETRIC_RELATION bridge. General type-family action B(a), symmetry,
composition, and univalence remain outside this rule.

The seven-field Universe correspondence currently stores A0, A1, R, trr, trl,
liftr, and liftl. It is a finite executable fibrancy interface, not a complete
higher bisimulation. In particular it does not yet store the higher-recursive
coherence field that makes the bisimulation structure itself stable under
identity. Consequently the manifest does not claim generic groupoid inversion,
composition, box filling, J, or full Higher Observational Type Theory.

Object term action for a Context variable is independent of the source type
former. It instantiates the exact family retained by the
IDENTITY_TYPE_COMPUTATION certificate at the two reindexed variable endpoints,
then uses the identity witness introduced with that Context binding. It does
not require a generated ADT identity declaration and therefore applies equally
to generated ADT families and direct pointwise Pi identity families. A mapped
witness may be converted only after the exact instantiated family has been
formed and checked.

Object action for a typed THUNK(LAMBDA(x,body)) at a direct pointwise Pi
identity is derivation-driven. It extends the outer object bridge by x0, x1,
and xR, composes the outer endpoint substitutions with the three-field
projection, and adds the source Lambda Binding identity to the same object
action environment. A RETURN(v) body recursively acts on v. A pure raw-CBPV
APP(FORCE(f),x) body recursively acts on f and x, applies the pointwise function
identity witness to x0, x1, and xR, and sequences its intermediate computation
results with zero-clause COMPUTATION_FOLD nodes. Generated intermediate
pointwise types receive ordinary structural type-formation DAGs. Convertible
but nonidentical specialized families are connected by an explicit CONVERSION
Derivation. Identity Claims inherited from the outer telescope are reindexed
into the pointwise body Context before use. The resulting ordinary three-Lambda
witness inhabits the exact endpoint-instantiated Pi family. Inspecting a shared
Core Lambda without its accepted THUNK/LAMBDA and body Derivations is not
authority for this action. Effectful APP and general computation bodies remain
residual.

Object action for THUNK(RETURN(v)) in a non-empty object bridge reads the
accepted THUNK_INTRO and RETURN_INTRO premises, acts on v under the same
endpoint substitutions, and applies the generated three-field thunk identity
constructor to v0, v1, and vR. The final classifier is the exact family
obtained by instantiating the identity-computation certificate at the two
reindexed thunk endpoints. A constant-family computation rule may reuse this
action only when its retained source carrier is a pure ThunkType; the rule name
alone does not reinterpret another generated identity declaration as CBPV.
The third field may use either an ordinary generated identity declaration or a
direct pointwise Pi identity family. The generated THUNK_RETURN declaration,
its action certificate, and accepted replay all validate that choice through
the one TypeDeclarationDB generated-identity validator; no HOTT-local duplicate
validator defines a narrower identity fragment.

Ordinary object action is recursively type-directed. Constructor fields,
RETURN values, and Lambda bodies enter one dispatcher which computes the exact
local identity family from the subterm classifier and the inherited object
bridge. Generated ADT/Thunk families and direct pointwise Pi families share
this path; no source-Term tag is treated as proof authority without its
accepted Derivation. If the two reindexed classifiers do not convert, or the
required dependent family lifting is unavailable, the subaction is residual
rather than replaced by compiler-local RELATION evidence.

Object action for a nullary ordinary Match is derivation-driven. The accepted
MATCH_ELIM classifier premise must itself have an accepted APP_ELIM derivation
that identifies the exact scrutinee Claim. The action recursively acts on that
scrutinee and every branch body, then eliminates the resulting indexed identity
witness with an ordinary indexed MATCH_ELIM. Its motive is the exact identity
family instantiated at the two endpoint Matches. Convertible source motives
are connected by explicit CONVERSION Claims; raw Term equality is not required.
This rule is the nullary base case only. Pattern fields, recursive IH, dependent
motives, and effectful branch computations remain residual.

For a supported closed unindexed ordinary ADT T, identity computation generates
an indexed ordinary declaration IdT : T -> T -> Universe. The two endpoints are
an index telescope, not uniform parameters. For every source constructor C with
fields a it generates one ordinary constructor CR whose telescope contains a0,
a1, and IdA(a0,a1) for each source field, and whose result is
IdT(C a0)(C a1). Nullary constructors are the empty-telescope case. For a
supported indexed-nullary source fiber, only source constructors whose exact
result classifier is that fiber generate constructors. Generated constructor
ordinals are local; replay derives the source ordinal from the two endpoint
constructor spines in the generated result classifier. No parallel provenance
table is authoritative. The generated declaration has exact source-carrier
provenance, and its unsaturated family is certified by the existing
TYPE_FORMATION_INTRO rule. The computation certificate additionally owns the
endpoint Context, its two binding identities, the concrete type IdT(x0,x1) in
that Context, and its exact formation Claim. The unsaturated former alone is
not a computed identity result. Distinct source constructors have no generated
identity constructor between them. This computes an identity family; it does
not fabricate an endpoint-only witness and does not extend DefEq.

The indexed-nullary closure is the first executable identity-of-identity case:
an ordinary proof p : IdBool(false,false) can be used as an endpoint of the
generated family Id_(IdBool(false,false))(p,p), and ordinary degeneracy builds
its constructor witness. This demonstrates one additional dimension without
proof irrelevance. Nondependent fields are also executable through the
four-corner, four-edge, one-center constructor telescope. It does not implement
general higher closure: dependent fields need identity-selected lifting through
their preceding field and index telescopes and remain residual.

For ThunkType(Comp(empty,A)), identity computation generates an indexed
ordinary declaration whose endpoints are thunk values. Its RETURN higher
constructor has fields v0:A, v1:A, and vR:IdA(v0,v1), and result indices
THUNK(RETURN(v0)) and THUNK(RETURN(v1)). This is the object realization of
computation equivalence at the pure returning computation type. It adds no
computation endpoint to ordinary type dependency; neutral or effectful
computations remain residual.

Observation planning is repeatable: an already interned candidate remains a
valid candidate even when a later planning run allocates no new record. The
work result is graph-consed by exact goal, normalization profile, step limit,
TermDB revision, and calculus fingerprint; source position is diagnostic data
and does not split the prior-computation result. The
plan-and-execute boundary starts exact Type actions and starts Term actions only
for exact diagonal candidates; forming an uninhabited distinct-constructor
family never fabricates an inhabitant.

For a same-constructor ordinary ADT action, the object witness remains
RELATION_WITNESS(left,right). Its exact Derivation is
RELATION_CONSTRUCTOR_WITNESS and contains one accepted field-witness Claim
per constructor argument in telescope order. Field evidence is proof authority,
not part of TermDB object identity. Recursive constructor action recursively
uses the same immutable Type and Term action requests.

For Comp(empty,A), RETURN action recursively acts on its value and records the
resulting witness Claim as an RELATION_RETURN_WITNESS premise. THUNK action
does the same for its enclosed pure computation using
RELATION_THUNK_WITNESS. Neither rule admits an effectful or unresolved row.

APP action recursively acts on its function and argument premises. Its exact
RELATION_APP_WITNESS derivation stores both child witness Claims. A child
witness may be any inhabitant of the generated relation type, including a
Context relation variable; it need not have RELATION_WITNESS object syntax.

LAMBDA action constructs or reuses the bridge for its binder Context. The body
witness lives under the ordered x0, x1, and input-relation extensions. Replay
requires that this Context extends the outer bridge Context by exactly those
three fields and that abstracting the body endpoints reconstructs both outer
Lambda endpoints up to shared Core alpha shape.

MATCH action recursively acts on its scrutinee and every branch body in the
relational bridge of that branch Context and records all child witnesses. A
Match whose branches share one graph body independent of all pattern binders is
a constant eliminator and reduces to that body under the ordinary Match
reduction profile, including for a neutral scrutinee.

Elimination of a generated nullary ADT identity family is indexed elimination,
not ordinary branch-hint checking. Each branch owns a Context substitution that
maps both endpoint indices and the relation witness to the exact result of the
selected higher constructor. The branch body and motive are reindexed through
that substitution. Accepted replay recomputes the canonical substitution and
rejects a branch edge carrying another constructor's solution. This first
fragment deliberately leaves indexed constructors with fields unsupported.

An RELATION_MATCH_WITNESS derivation records the accepted source Match Claim
in addition to both endpoint Match Claims, the scrutinee witness, and every
branch witness. Branch witnesses act on the source branch body under the
left/right branch Context extensions. The enclosing Match derivation closes the
source IH frame against the independently reindexed endpoint Match frames; an
IH frame ID is never treated as an ordinary binder ID or silently renamed by a
branch-local substitution.

INDUCTION_HYPOTHESIS action is guarded by an accepted source
INDUCTION_HYPOTHESIS_ELIM Claim and the relation witness of its recursive
argument. It does not recursively invoke the enclosing Match action and cannot
introduce a cycle in the Derivation DAG.

A substitution action owns a typed naturality certificate for both endpoint
squares under an exact pure conversion profile and deterministic step budget.
Exhaustion is residual and never equality. Definitional conversion remains
meta-level evidence and successful object proofs never extend global DefEq.
Reindexing a Claim along the identity Context substitution returns that Claim
itself. It does not add a SUBSTITUTION_REINDEX derivation with the same Claim as
both conclusion and premise; accepted evidence remains a DAG.

Family formation and family inhabitation are distinct. REL_ADT_DISTINCT forms
an EMPTY_FAMILY candidate; it is not a witness and not compiler contradiction.
Candidate object results distinguish WITNESS construction, EMPTY_FAMILY
computation, and a DEFERRED object rule even when relation-family planning is
otherwise ready. Work
items and residual obligations are compiler-local and are not artifact roots
in fragment version 2.
